    <!-- ============================ Onboarding (unified style) ============================ -->
    <string name="onboarding_intro">Hi! Meha is an AI agent that controls your phone. Set up the connection to a model and we will get started.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_model_title">Model</string>
    <string name="onboarding_models_hint_fill">Enter the endpoint and API key — the model list will load automatically.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_local_note">You can work fully offline with a model on the device: it is downloaded once and needs no internet. It is configured in Settings; requires ≥ 11 GB of RAM.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_permissions_title">Permissions</string>
    <string name="onboarding_permissions_body">Permissions are requested as they are used — the first time the agent needs the matching tool. The full list and controls are on the \"All permissions\" screen in settings. You can deny any permission — then the agent simply cannot use that tool. On Android 13+, the system may refuse to enable Accessibility or Notification access: open the app info page and tap ⋮ → \"Allow restricted settings\".</string>
